nodecode-local-mcp is a rewrite of colibird-ai's colibird-ai/local-mcp-hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/colibird-ai/local-mcp-hermes-plugin
  commit 6d6da7722af2243aa6f92fc363405c629e162cf6
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Colibird (LICENSE)

The original is a launcher and a skill: a root plugin.json and mcp.json that
start the MCP server bundled inside the separately installed LMCP app with
LMCP_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1, a fourteen-line shell launcher that looks in
~/Applications and /Applications for either bundle name and downloads
nothing, and skills/local-mcp/SKILL.md, which teaches scoping tools for
unattended jobs, the confirm flow for calls that send or cannot be undone,
and treating app content as untrusted data. The rewrite carries all three:
client.lisp is the launcher and the MCP client the original left to Hermes
(same two app directories and bundle names, same --auto argument, same
telemetry variable), and the skill's rules are the manual topic, its scoping
turned into the section's include and exclude lists.

What was left out: the original registers every tool the server lists, one
per tool, because Hermes's MCP client does. A cell is alone in its folder
and reaches Nodecode's tool catalog directly, so the catalog stays data that
local_mcp_tools answers and local_mcp_call runs; registering two hundred
schemas would put all of them in every prompt, which is what the include
list exists to prevent. Nothing else of the original is omitted, and no code
is shared: this is a Common Lisp reimplementation against the MCP wire
(JSON-RPC over the server's stdio), not a copy of the plugin.
